{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Behold, etc.</b> This is the land of the Chaldeans, and the meaning concerns its inhabitants." "<b>This people.</b> That is, the people of the Chaldeans." "<b>It was not.</b> Like it, and similarly לא היה פחד (Psalms 53:5). Some say it means 'Would that it were not,' for behold, the kingdom of <b>Assyria founded it.</b> The meaning is that He made it a dwelling for jackals [ציים], that is, the beasts that are in the land." "<b>[They set up its towers].</b> Even though those who set up Assyria's towers did so for warfare, like Ophel and Bohen (Isaiah 32:14), and it is a lofty structure — the correct reading is that the vav of בחוניו refers back to the people of the Chaldeans: 'as the one who set up its towers' — they roused [עוררו], a transitive verb, as if those who roused [המבחונים] stirred up the palaces until they were roused — to ruin there."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:54:51.933139321Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}